SUN - SPARC - UNIX  
—  OBJECTIVE BRIEF
(era of the vintage OpenWindows + Netscape Communicator 4.75 screenshot)

COMPANY
  Sun Microsystems, Inc.   founded 1982
  Name from Stanford University Network
  Founders: Andy Bechtolsheim, Vinod Khosla, Scott McNealy, Bill Joy
  Acquired by Oracle 2010
  Slogan: "The network is the computer"

UNIX LINEAGE
  Type: multiuser, multitasking, networked OS
  Path: BSD Unix  ->  SunOS (BSD-based)  ->  Solaris (SVR4 base + Sun engineering)
  Solaris: enterprise Unix, NFS, later ZFS / DTrace / zones
  File sharing standard: NFS (1984)

SPARC  (Scalable Processor ARChitecture)
  Type: RISC ISA  (Reduced Instruction Set Computer)
  Introduced: 1987   first systems: Sun-4 / SPARCstation line 1987-1989
  Style: load-store (register-register)
  All arithmetic/logic on registers; memory only via load/store
  Word: 32-bit (V7/V8) then 64-bit (V9 / UltraSPARC)
  Integer unit (IU) + optional FPU
  Register windows (Berkeley RISC heritage):
    visible set: 32 integer registers
      %g0..%g7   globals     (%g0 hardwired 0)
      %o0..%o7   outs
      %l0..%l7   locals
      %i0..%i7   ins
    window slide on call/return reduces memory traffic
  Open ISA; licensed implementations (Fujitsu, Cypress, TI, later Oracle)

